      "writtenOn": "2024-08-21T15:25:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Curious what you think about this. The bug reporter is able to just patch the size limit, so this isn\u0027t strictly necessary. Also, we could add an option (via SkRuntimneEffect::Options, that routes to ProgramSettings). But I wondered why we were still enforcing the limit at all -- we no longer have SkVM, and the RP SkSL backend doesn\u0027t unroll loops, so the size limit is fairly arbitrary. Perhaps something terrible happens if we stop enforcing it? I can\u0027t see what, though.",
      "revId": "6c05bc35b0953d9e912ef241b9667c6044a58bbf",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
