      "writtenOn": "2024-08-21T15:38:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Assuming that this limitation was truly because of SkVM and unrolling, I prefer the simplicity of this validation being based on stack depth and function call cycles. I believe the inliner already has program size guards in place that are applied universally.\n\nIf something newly terrible happens, I would characterize it as a latent bug within the sksl compiler or rp backend that is worth fixing regardless of whether or not this program size shield is kept.\n\nI definitely like the end user behavior of not having arbitrary limits that are hard to predict. Even with the program limits, you could create exceedingly slow CPU sksl programs so I think that just reflects the sharpness of the tool.",
      "parentUuid": "091b9a6b_7b0b1183",
      "revId": "6c05bc35b0953d9e912ef241b9667c6044a58bbf",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
